        "key": "retrograde",
        "name": "Retrograde",
        "works": 10,
        "definition": "The ranks run n … 3, 2, 1 throughout, and there is no present-day scene the narrative keeps returning to.",
        "description": "The telling runs backwards: a descending staircase, not a descending line. Scenes are told in reverse order while each scene plays forward inside itself. The pure reversal is the shape no work in the corpus has and the one models produce when instructed.",
        "example": "The color strand of Memento offers a familiar example: successive scenes lead back to earlier events.",
        "exampleWorks": [
          "Memento"
